From: lfdevs <lfdevs@lfdevs.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:11:24 +0800
Subject: obs-ffmpeg: support termux-va in DRM-less containers

Share VA-API device selection between media sources and encoder discovery. Honor OBS_VAAPI_DEVICE and select /dev/kgsl-3d0 when the termux-va bridge uses the KGSL backend, while preserving ordinary DRM discovery otherwise.

Expose the selected device in encoder properties and report successful hardware decoder initialization. Route KGSL texture encoders through synchronized CPU readback and VA-API upload: glFlush alone leaves cross-context DMA-BUF reads unsynchronized, causing green startup frames and stale pictures. MediaCodec still performs hardware encoding.

Document setup and the tested AVC, HEVC and VP9 decoding paths, AVC/HEVC recording, and the remaining AV1 media-source limitation.

Validated with a native Arm64 obs-ffmpeg build in Debian 13 PRoot on Xiaomi Pad 6 Pro, real OBS recordings and frame-content comparisons, hardware session logs, and device-selection assertions.
